WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.700
We're learning what

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.968
Tucker Carlson texted

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.169
that was so worrisome

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.170
to Fox executives

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:04.738
and the board

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:05.505
that it reportedly

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.906
contributed to his firing.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.475
The New York Times reported

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.409
on the message,

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.644
which was sent on January seven. 20, 21.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.812
Obviously, a pivotal day

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.214
right after the insurrection,

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:14.848
just hours

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.182
after those riots at the Capitol.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.751
And he was talking about a video

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.618
he saw of Trump

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.452
supporters

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.055
beating up, in his words, and Antifa kid.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.424
It was redacted in the Dominion

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.525
lawsuit, court filings.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.126
But here's

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.261
what part of the Times says is behind

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.796
that big black box

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.865
at the bottom right of those filings.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.767
A quote from Tucker's

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.201
text, it read, quote,

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.569
It was three against one,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.670
at least jumping.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.606
A guy like that is dishonorable.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.242
Obviously, it's not how white men fight.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:42.976
Yet suddenly

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.077
I found myself rooting

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.812
for the mob against the man, hoping

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.847
they'd hit him harder, kill him.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.916
I really wanted them to hurt the kid.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.051
I could taste it.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.552
Then somewhere deep in my brain,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.486
an alarm went off.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.788
This isn't good for me.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:55.722
I'm becoming something

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.857
I don't want to be. Close quote.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.492
The Times is only able to unveil

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.126
the contents

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.428
of that text through interviews

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.195
with people

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.264
who spoke on the condition of anonymity.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.032
CNN reached out for comment.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.000
Fox declined.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.269
Carlson did not immediately respond Back

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:09.469
with us

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:09.903
now, a writer

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.104
at large for The New York Times,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:11.738
Jim Rittenberg,

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.473
who helped break this story.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.641
We were talking about, you know,

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.842
there's no

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.943
you can't just say, yes,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.478
this is ultimately what led to it.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.013
But it's also the way that this came out

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.148
and how executives found out about this.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.116
And we're seeing this message

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:23.817
right before they were

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.518
set to go to trial.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.353
What is the impact that that had of

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.322
when they learned about this?

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.757
Well, as we understand

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.325
it, the board going

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.226
the trial was supposed

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.594
to start on a Monday

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.162
going into that weekend.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.298
The board had asked to see

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.766
some of the redacted messages

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.533
in negotiations

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.868
about a potential settlement.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.504
The jury is coming together. So the board

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:46.339
starts going

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.340
through the messages,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.008
finds this one message

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.210
that they find very troubling.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.678
Some senior executives were told

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.613
hadn't been focused on this message.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.316
And it's not what you want to see

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.384
when you're going into trial.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.385
A jury is being impaneled

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.487
and you're negotiating

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.122
what's going to be a potentially

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.623
very high number

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.457
to get out of this

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.191
so you don't

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.326
have to put something like this

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.660
in front of a jury.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.329
But for this

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.431
text message being revealed to the

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.232
to the board

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.166
and Fox executives

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:13.967
the night before

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.835
the trial was supposed to begin,

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:16.803
would there have been a trial

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.204
and no settlement

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.372
I still

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.940
they were definitely working

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.674
toward a settlement.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.510
And we were told that over the weekend,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.310
Lachlan Murdoch,

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.879
one of the leaders of the company,

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.646
had told his lawyers,

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.981
let's start moving up on the number

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:28.848
to get out of this anyway.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.949
I mean, that trial was going

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.818
to be potentially disastrous

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.153
on so many levels.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.587
So but here again, you see,

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.422
when it comes to Tucker Carlson,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.023
the issue here

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.992
is that he's he's playing an outsize role

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:41.194
in terms of problems in the case for them

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.162
when he's really not

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.096
a huge part of the case.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.831
And that represents the trouble

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:45.698
with Tucker Carlson

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.467
to management at this point,

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.868
among other things,

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:49.669
and the questions

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:50.236
that are made

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.005
of why they did not settle sooner,

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.040
because all of this damaging information

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:54.841
came out, though

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.642
obviously this came out

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.076
as a part of good reporting.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.044
Abby Grosberg

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.445
is the former Fox News producer

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.681
who is now suing the network,

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.750
and she was on with Anderson last night.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.918
She was talking about

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.219
essentially the way things worked

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.453
and when it came to the fight

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.321
that we all watch play out

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:08.988
so dramatically

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.757
in Washington over Kevin McCarthy

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.625
and his bid to become House speaker,

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:13.626
she said this is what they talked

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.527
about behind the scenes

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.798
They believed that he could broker

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.233
who was speaker.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:20.867
House speaker.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.302
He wanted to do that live on air.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.837
But Kevin McCarthy said no.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:25.738
What do you mean

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.607
he wanted to do that live on air?

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.343
His plan was to have Kevin McCarthy

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.311
come on the show.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.946
So fast forward to January 5th.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.280
They start asking me to book

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.582
McCarthy on the show that night.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.417
I had worked with him

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:37.917
a lot

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.252
when I was at Sunday Morning Futures

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:42.021
and had a relationship with his team.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.623
That afternoon, Justin came in

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.124
and he said, here's a plan

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.260
Tucker is going to first have Kevin on.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.429
Hear him beg and grovel.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.064
Then we'll bring in Matt Gates.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.398
And Matt Gates

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.601
will then kind of set his terms

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.469
Then Tucker will set his terms

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.404
that McCarthy has to agree to.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:01.174
Carlson had terms in the terms terms,

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.509
and we're going to make this whole thing

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.110
happen on air

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.845
and save the Republican Party.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.548
Now, fortunately, for McCarthy's sake,

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.949
he said no,

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.685
he speaks a level of influence.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.653
I mean, that's why

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.088
this is in a way, so shocking.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:16.089
Look at that

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.624
level of political influence

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.691
that Tucker Carlson had.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:18.958
I mean,

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.628
he was a power in the part of the party

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:22.862
that it's the tail

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.230
wagging the dog right now.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.799
And so to suddenly be cut,

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:27.700
it's really amazing.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.936
But that shows also this symbiosis

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.837
that could happen

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.138
with the Fox prime time

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.573
and people in power

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.141
particularly Republicans.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.542
We saw it with the Trump White House.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.577
So here you see it again.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.212
Yeah.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.947
Jim, again,

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:41.914
as Kaitlan said, this came

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:42.849
because of good

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.617
reporting to you and your team. Kudos.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:45.285
Thank you.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:45.852
Thanks for having me.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:46.919
Thanks for joining us.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:47.787
Let's talk about this

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:48.655
